Adam Trace Spragg wrote on 07/30/2003 12:42 AM:
> Anyone who's played Freecell on Windows will know that you can start a
> game either with a random number, or you can provide your own number as
> a seed.
> 
> Has anyone tried modifying Nethack's seeding of the RNG?

IIRC Nethack uses the current time in some form as a seed. It's fairly
easy to change this if you wish, but it would be a bit pointless. The
effect might be not what you expected--remember that the dungeon is
created as you play, so I think the only common thing between
incarnations would be the first level (if you don't explicitly prevent
this by choosing another race, role, etc.). You must not save/restore
the game and repeat each action exactly to get the same game.

With Freecell it's just a convenient way to restart a game which didn't
go well. In Nethack, savescumming would be an easier way if you desire
exactly the same starting circumstances.

